Add a review to a GitHub pull request. review is required for REQUEST_CHANGES and COMMENT events.

```ts
mcp__GitHub__add_review_to_pr(args: // add_review_to_pr_input
{
// Repo Full Name
//
// Repository in `owner/name` form, such as `openai/openai`. This maps to GitHub REST `owner` and `repo` path parameters: https://docs.github.com/en/rest/repos/repos#get-a-repository
repo_full_name: string,
// Pr Number
//
// Pull request number in the repository.
pr_number: integer,
// GithubReviewAction
//
// Review action to take. `review` is required for `COMMENT` and `REQUEST_CHANGES`.
action: "COMMENT" | "APPROVE" | "REQUEST_CHANGES",
// Review
//
// Review body to submit. Required when requesting changes or leaving a comment.
review?: string | null, // default: null
// File Comments
//
// Optional inline file comments to include with the review.
// default: null
file_comments?:
 | Array<
// GithubFileComment
{
// Path
//
// Repository path of the file to comment on.
path: string,
// Position
//
// The position in the diff where you want to add a review comment. Note this value is not the same as the line number in the file. The position value equals the number of lines down from the first "@@" hunk header in the file you want to add a comment. The line just below the "@@" line is position 1, the next line is position 2, and so on. The position in the diff continues to increase through lines of whitespace and additional hunks until the beginning of a new file.
position?: integer | null, // default: null
// Body
//
// Body text for the review comment.
body: string,
// Line
//
// File line number for line-based review comments.
line?: integer | null, // default: null
// Side
//
// Diff side for `line`, such as `LEFT` or `RIGHT`.
side?: string | null, // default: null
// Start Line
//
// Starting line number for a multi-line review comment range.
start_line?: integer | null, // default: null
// Start Side
//
// Diff side for `start_line`, such as `LEFT` or `RIGHT`.
start_side?: string | null, // default: null
}
>
 | null
,
// Commit Id
//
// Optional commit SHA to anchor the review.
commit_id?: string | null, // default: null
}): Promise<// add_review_to_pr_output
{
// GithubReviewResponse
result: {
// Success
//
// Whether the review operation completed successfully.
success: boolean,
// Review Id
//
// Identifier of the created or updated review, when available.
review_id?: string | integer | null, // default: null
},
}>;
```

Compare two commits/refs and return per-file stats plus compare metadata. This is a thin wrapper around `GithubPlugin.compare_commits` to provide a stable, compact response shape to connector consumers.

```ts
mcp__GitHub__compare_commits(args: // compare_commits_input
{
// Repo Full Name
repo_full_name: string,
// Base
base: string,
// Head
head: string,
}): Promise<// compare_commits_output
{
// GithubCompareCommitsResult
//
// Minimal, stable subset of `GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/compare/{base}...{head}`.
//
// Consumers generally only need commit refs + ahead/behind counts and per-file stats
// (changes/additions/deletions).
result: {
// Repository Full Name
repository_full_name: string,
// Base
base: string,
// Head
head: string,
// Status
status?: string | null, // default: null
// Ahead By
ahead_by?: integer | null, // default: null
// Behind By
behind_by?: integer | null, // default: null
// Total Commits
total_commits?: integer | null, // default: null
// Too Large
too_large?: boolean | null, // default: null
// default: null
base_commit?:
// GithubCompareCommitRef
//
// A lightweight commit reference used by compare endpoints.
 | {
// Sha
sha: string,
// Url
url?: string | null, // default: null
// Html Url
html_url?: string | null, // default: null
}
 | null
,
// default: null
merge_base_commit?:
// GithubCompareCommitRef
//
// A lightweight commit reference used by compare endpoints.
 | {
// Sha
sha: string,
// Url
url?: string | null, // default: null
// Html Url
html_url?: string | null, // default: null
}
 | null
,
// Files
// default: []
files?: Array<
// GithubCompareFileStats
//
// Per-file change stats returned by the compare endpoint.
{
// Filename
filename: string,
// Status
status?: string | null, // default: null
// Additions
additions?: integer | null, // default: null
// Deletions
deletions?: integer | null, // default: null
// Changes
changes?: integer | null, // default: null
// Previous Filename
previous_filename?: string | null, // default: null
}
>,
},
}>;
```

